Flutter's `Form` widget groups `TextFormField`s and coordinates validation. Attach a `GlobalKey<FormState>`, give each field a `validator` that returns an error string or `null`, then call `formKey.currentState!.validate()` on submit — it runs every field's validator and shows errors inline.

```dart
final _formKey = GlobalKey<FormState>();

Form(
  key: _formKey,
  child: TextFormField(
    validator: (v) => (v == null || v.isEmpty) ? 'Required' : null,
  ),
);

// on submit:
if (_formKey.currentState!.validate()) { /* proceed */ }
```
`autovalidateMode` controls whether validation reruns on every change vs. only on submit/interaction.

