When built-in widgets can't express a shape (a custom chart, a progress ring, a signature pad), `CustomPaint` + a `CustomPainter` subclass draw directly to a `Canvas` using low-level primitives (`drawLine`, `drawPath`, `drawArc`, ...).

```dart
class RingPainter extends CustomPainter {
  RingPainter(this.progress);
  final double progress;

  @override
  void paint(Canvas canvas, Size size) {
    final paint = Paint()..strokeWidth = 8..style = PaintingStyle.stroke;
    canvas.drawArc(Offset.zero & size, -1.57, 6.28 * progress, false, paint);
  }

  @override
  bool shouldRepaint(covariant RingPainter old) => old.progress != progress;
}
```
`shouldRepaint` is important — returning `true` unconditionally repaints every frame even with no visual change, hurting performance.

